WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.002
GAVIN NEWSOME:
 I think it's always more fun
 having the conservative guests

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.270
and having that back and forth.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.239
In fact, that's what makes,
I think, the show work.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.742
I agree with you about labels,
but I notice you're sitting

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.211
in front of a billboard
that says Runaway Slave.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:14.080
I don't have time
to go through all of his lies,

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.215
we only have an hour.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.684
-Uh... But let's--
-(AUDIENCE CHEERS)

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.919
I can bat them all down. Go.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.287
I think you're a great guy,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.989
I really hope you lose
your next election,

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.424
-because I think you're wrong
about everything.
-(AUDIENCE CHEERS)

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.394
I think you're colossally wrong
on a number of things.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.162
-That's okay.
-But if-- Exactly.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.664
-We're allowed to disagree
on things.
-If I banned everyone

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.800
from my show who I thought
was colossally wrong,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.568
I would be talking to myself.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.437
S.E. CUPP:
 I think it's important,

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.672
especially when you think
someone is dangerous,

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.375
to expose that
to as many people as you can.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:47.046
So giving someone like Milo
or Alex Jones, or Anne Coulter,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.250
a platform,
that's a public service.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.252
You said after 9/11
what we should do

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.788
is attack Muslim countries,
kill their leaders,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.289
and convert them
to Christianity.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.158
-Yes.
-Do you... Do you still stand

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.327
-by that moderate position?
-Absolutely fantastic policy,
I haven't heard a better one.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.364
I love people
who stick by their guns,

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:07.133
even when the crowd
does not agree.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.236
I do think that there's
an element of racism

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.439
against white individuals,
I do.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.675
-I do see it, I think it's--
-Well, since I'm a conservative
and not a Trump person,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.643
let me just say this.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.046
-That's absurd.
That's fucking crazy.
-(AUDIENCE CHEERS)

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.283
The Pope
made a very strong statement

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.719
in support of my position
on climate change, not yours.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.222
And your position
when you heard that was,

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.958
hey, let's leave the science
to the scientists.

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:33.993
Okay, first of all,
you're not doing that.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.296
-But second of all...
-I am.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.399
You're not, because 97 percent
of all scientists believe...

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:40.567
It's a bogus number.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.435
-It's so not a bogus number.
-It's so a bogus number.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.237
Okay, yours is, mine is,
yours is, mine is.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:45.438
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.841
This show, like none other,
provides an opportunity

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.610
to articulate
deeply held beliefs,

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.646
cherished ideas,
in the face of people

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.381
who are radically skeptical
about them.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:57.484
Hold on,
relax, liberal audience.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.619
Let him get his bullshit out
before you boo him!

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.421
-(LAUGHS)
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.989
Thank you for having me
on this show

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.891
to present the other side,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.726
but not every network
does that all the time.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.529
This might be
the only place in the world

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.432
-where we'd ever meet.
-(LAUGHING)

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.901
Everyone knows that
he gives people room to breathe,

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.903
and he gives people
their time to talk

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.938
and make their point, um...

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:20.807
and he will give you your space
to do that.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.609
But then when you look
at the Democrats,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:25.245
you see who's up
against this guy,

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:29.115
this unbelievably useless,
terrible candidate

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.117
-of Hillary Clinton.
-(AUDIENCE BOOS)

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.586
I feel liberated to say
whatever I believe.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.122
And some of that
is not very popular,

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.758
I've gotten booed
several times by the audience.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.827
BARNEY FRANK: Bill is clearly
 someone who's liberal,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.495
but he's not a party line guy.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:46.299
You don't do your political
viewpoint party ideology

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.135
any favors if you assume
they're always right.

